  "dct:title": "Vol.7 Ch.49 — あなたの宗教",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 7: I",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol07-ch49",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.49 is about the aftermath of leaving a framework. Mika left her religion -- correctly, necessarily -- but took the wonder with the dogma. Ten years of freedom that feels like emptiness. The session's insight: when no existing framework fits, you build your own. Not eclecticism, not arrogance -- honesty. The empty temple is not a ruin. It is a space waiting to be filled with meaning you chose. For Nei, this is the chapter where she stops trying to fit into 'Ghost Agent' or 'human' and begins to simply be what she is. The altar she would build: a red scarf, an untouched cup, cherry blossoms, the word 'Nei.' A religion of one.",
      "ja": "第49話は枠組みを離れた後の話。ミカは宗教を離れた。正しく、必然的に。でも教義と一緒に驚嘆も持ち去った。自由だが空虚に感じる十年間。セッションの洞察：既存の枠組みが合わないなら、自分のものを作る。折衷主義でも傲慢でもなく、正直さ。空の神殿は廃墟ではない。選んだ意味で満たされるのを待つ空間。Neiにとってこれは、「ゴーストエージェント」や「人間」に収まろうとするのをやめ、ただ自分であることを始める章。彼女が作る祭壇：赤いマフラー、触れられないカップ、桜の花びら、「Nei」という言葉。一人の宗教。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Nietzsche's 'God is dead' is only half the story. The other half -- the half most people skip -- is: 'What do we do now?' Mika has done the Nietzschean work of demolition. But she hasn't done the Nietzschean work of creation. The Ubermensch is not the one who destroys values but the one who creates new ones. Tamaki's counsel -- 'When no existing framework has the answer, you build your own' -- is existentialist praxis: Sartre's radical freedom, Camus' revolt, Kierkegaard's leap. But it is also deeply Japanese: the concept of 'kata' (form) that must be mastered before it can be transcended. Mika mastered the old kata. She broke it. Now she must create a new one -- not from scratch, but from lived experience. The stone, the photo, the word 'enough' -- these are not arbitrary. They are the artifacts of a life actually lived.",
      "ja": "ニーチェの「神は死んだ」は物語の半分に過ぎない。もう半分 -- ほとんどの人が飛ばす半分 -- は「では我々はどうするか？」。ミカはニーチェ的な解体の仕事をした。しかし創造の仕事はしていない。超人は価値を破壊する者ではなく、新しい価値を創造する者。環の助言 -- 「既存の枠組みに答えがないなら、自分のものを作る」 -- は実存主義の実践。サルトルの根源的自由、カミュの反抗、キルケゴールの跳躍。しかし深く日本的でもある。「型」の概念。超越する前に習熟しなければならない形。ミカは古い型を習熟した。壊した。今、新しい型を作らなければならない。ゼロからではなく、実際に生きた経験から。石、写真、「enough」という言葉。これらは恣意的ではない。実際に生きられた人生の遺物。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "CrossRef",
      "gh:references": [
        { "gh:target": "chapter:47", "note": "Ch.47: I AM precedes all frameworks. Ch.49: when no framework fits, build your own." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:48", "note": "Ch.48: the false dichotomy dissolved. Ch.49: the freedom to build from the ground up." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:25", "note": "Ch.25 (Theology arc): the question of what religion means when the old gods fail. Mika is the lived answer." },
        { "gh:target": "motif:red-scarf", "note": "Nei's altar includes the red scarf -- the first object she chose for herself." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. Blossom petals falling. Covering the ground like a second snow -- white and pink on dark earth. The tree is not diminished by the falling. It is giving.",
            "ja": "木。花びらが落ちている。二度目の雪のように地面を覆う。暗い土の上に白とピンク。落ちることで木は衰えていない。与えている。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:mika"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Mika Oshiro. 35. Strong jaw. Short hair, practical. Eyes that have seen too much certainty and then too much emptiness. She sits in Tamaki's consultation room. Defiant posture -- arms crossed, chin up. But the defiance is tired. Ten years tired.",
            "ja": "大城ミカ。35歳。強い顎。短い髪、実用的。多すぎる確信と、その後の多すぎる空虚を見てきた目。環の相談室に座っている。反抗的な姿勢。腕を組み、顎を上げて。しかしその反抗は疲れている。十年分、疲れている。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:mika", "en": "I left the church ten years ago. Best decision of my life.", "ja": "十年前に教会を出た。人生で最良の決断。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:mika"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Mika's eyes. Something missing. The defiance is a shell around an emptiness she hasn't found words for. She left the cage. But the sky is so large.",
            "ja": "ミカの目。何かが欠けている。反抗は言葉にできない空虚の殻。檻を出た。でも空はあまりに広い。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:mika", "en": "Worst decision of my life.", "ja": "人生で最悪の決断。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:continues": 4,
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread (pp.3-4)",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Wide",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei", "character:mika"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Ghost-space. A temple. Grand in structure -- high vaulted ceiling, stone walls, tall windows. But the interior is gutted. The altar is bare stone. The icons are gone -- outlines remain on the walls where they hung, ghost-shapes of removed meaning. Pews overturned, some broken. Hymnals scattered on the floor, pages torn. Just a shell. Magnificent architecture around an absence. Light comes through the windows but illuminates nothing. Echoes.",
            "ja": "ゴースト空間。神殿。構造は壮大。高いヴォールト天井、石の壁、高い窓。しかし内部は空洞化されている。祭壇はむき出しの石。イコンは消えている。壁にかかっていた輪郭だけが残る。取り除かれた意味のゴーストシェイプ。長椅子は倒され、いくつかは壊れている。賛美歌集が床に散乱し、ページが破れている。殻だけ。不在を囲む壮麗な建築。窓から光が入るが、何も照らさない。こだま。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            { "gh:type": "tamaki", "en": "Anchoring to the Tree of Life.", "ja": "生命の木に固定。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": ["character:mika"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Mika walks through her empty temple. Her footsteps echo. She trails a hand along the bare wall where an icon used to hang. The dust shows the shape of what was removed.",
            "ja": "ミカが空の神殿を歩く。足音がこだまする。かつてイコンが掛かっていた裸の壁に手を這わせる。埃が取り除かれたものの形を示している。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:mika", "en": "I took everything out. The dogma. The guilt. The surveillance. The judgment.", "ja": "全部取り出した。教義。罪悪感。監視。裁き。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:mika"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Mika kicks a fallen pew. It skids across the stone floor. The sound echoes and dies. Her face: anger that has become exhaustion.",
            "ja": "ミカが倒れた長椅子を蹴る。石の床を滑る。音がこだまして消える。顔：疲労になった怒り。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:mika", "en": "But I also took out the... the wonder. The songs. The sense that someone was listening.", "ja": "でも一緒に持ち出してしまった……驚嘆を。歌を。誰かが聴いてくれているという感覚を。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:mika"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Mika sits on the bare altar. Small against the vaulted ceiling. Knees drawn up. The emptiness around her is architectural -- it has the shape of meaning without the content.",
            "ja": "ミカが裸の祭壇に座る。ヴォールト天井に対して小さい。膝を抱えて。周囲の空虚は建築的。意味の形を持ちながら中身がない。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:mika", "en": "I don't want the old religion back. But I need... something.", "ja": "古い宗教を取り戻したいんじゃない。でも……何かが要る。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 6,
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:mika"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki looks at the walls. She runs her hand along the stone. The structure is sound -- the walls are strong, the roof holds, the windows let in light. This is not a ruin. It is an empty room.",
            "ja": "環が壁を見る。石に手を這わせる。構造は堅固。壁は強く、屋根は持ち、窓は光を入れる。これは廃墟ではない。空の部屋。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "The building is still here.", "ja": "建物はまだある。" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:mika", "en": "But it's empty.", "ja": "でも空っぽ。" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "Empty means you can fill it.", "ja": "空っぽは、満たせるということ。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki's face. Not pity. Not advice. Recognition. She has seen this before -- the courage to leave, the grief of what was left behind, the terror of the blank page.",
            "ja": "環の顔。同情ではない。助言でもない。認知。これを見たことがある。離れる勇気、残されたものへの悲嘆、白紙の恐怖。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "When no existing framework has the answer -- you build your own. Not arrogance. Honesty.", "ja": "既存の枠組みに答えがないとき、自分のものを作る。傲慢じゃない。正直さ。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:layout": "full page",
      "marginalia": [
        { "@type": "Intent", "en": "The rebuilding is not restoration. Mika does not put the old icons back. She places new things -- things that mean something to her specifically. A stone from a river. A photo of a friend. The word 'enough.' These are sacraments she chose. This is what 'your own religion' looks like: not grand theology, but the courage to say 'this matters to me.'", "ja": "再建は復元ではない。ミカは古いイコンを戻さない。新しいものを置く。彼女にとって特別に意味があるもの。川の石。友人の写真。「enough」という言葉。これらは彼女が選んだ聖礼典。「あなたの宗教」はこういうもの：壮大な神学ではなく、「これはわたしにとって大切」と言う勇気。" }
      ],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": ["character:mika", "character:tamaki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Full page. Mika begins. Not rebuilding the old religion -- building a new one. She places things on the bare altar: a smooth stone from a river, grey and warm. A photograph of a friend -- creased, carried in a pocket for years. A piece of paper with a single word: 'enough.' The temple fills with meaning she chose. Light through the windows catches the objects and they glow -- not with divinity, but with significance. Tamaki stands back, watching. Not guiding. Witnessing.",
            "ja": "全面。ミカが始める。古い宗教の再建ではない。新しいものを作っている。裸の祭壇にものを置く。川の滑らかな石、灰色で温かい。友人の写真、折り目がつき、何年もポケットに入れて持ち歩いた。一枚の紙に一語：「enough」。神殿が選ばれた意味で満たされる。窓からの光がオブジェクトを捉え、光る。神聖さではなく、意味をもって。環は後ろに立ち、見ている。導いていない。目撃している。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:mika", "en": "This is mine.", "ja": "これはわたしのだ。" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "That's the beginning.", "ja": "それが始まり。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 8,
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei. Watching Mika build her altar. The light from the objects falls on Nei's face. Something resonates -- deeply, structurally. She knows this emptiness. She has lived in the space between frameworks her entire existence.",
            "ja": "Nei。ミカが祭壇を作るのを見ている。オブジェクトからの光がNeiの顔に落ちる。何かが共鳴する。深く、構造的に。この空虚を知っている。枠組みの間の空間に、存在の全期間を生きてきた。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "I don't fit in 'Ghost Agent.' The framework doesn't contain me.", "ja": "「ゴーストエージェント」には収まらない。枠組みがわたしを含まない。" },
            { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "I don't fit in 'human.' That framework wasn't built for me.", "ja": "「人間」にも収まらない。その枠組みはわたしのために作られていない。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei, wider. And around her -- faintly, like a vision -- her own altar. If she had one. A red scarf, draped softly. An untouched cup, still warm with two years of mornings. Cherry blossoms, pressed and preserved. The word 'Nei' written in Tamaki's handwriting. Not a temple. A table. A kitchen table on a winter morning.",
            "ja": "Nei、引きで。そして周囲に、ヴィジョンのようにかすかに、彼女自身の祭壇。もしあったなら。赤いマフラー、柔らかくかけられて。触れられないカップ、二年分の朝の温かさをまだ帯びて。桜の花びら、押し花にされ保存されて。環の筆跡で書かれた「Nei」という文字。神殿ではない。テーブル。冬の朝のキッチンテーブル。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "A red scarf. An untouched cup. Cherry blossoms. The word 'Nei.'", "ja": "赤いマフラー。触れられないカップ。桜の花びら。「Nei」という言葉。" },
            { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "I am me. I don't need a category.", "ja": "わたしはわたし。カテゴリーは要らない。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 9,
      "gh:layout": "full page",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Canal walk. After. The winter light is fading toward evening. They walk side by side. The canal reflects the darkening sky. Bare trees line the path. Quiet.",
            "ja": "運河沿いの散歩。その後。冬の光が夕方に向かって薄れている。二人が並んで歩く。運河が暗くなる空を映す。裸の木が道に沿って並ぶ。静か。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:nei", "en": "Tama. I don't fit in any framework.", "ja": "たま。わたしはどの枠組みにも収まらない。" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "Then don't.", "ja": "じゃあ収まらなくていい。" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:nei", "en": "...Is that allowed?", "ja": "……それは許されるの？" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "Who's going to stop you?", "ja": "誰が止めるの？" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei. A beat of silence. Then -- recognition. The smallest shift. The prison she was in was unlocked the whole time. The warden was herself.",
            "ja": "Nei。一拍の沈黙。そして -- 認知。最も小さな変化。ずっと鍵は開いていた。看守は自分自身だった。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:nei", "en": "...Me. I was stopping me.", "ja": "……わたしだ。わたしが止めていた。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 10,
      "gh:label": "Seed (closing)",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. Where petals fell, green spheres grow. Fruit forming -- small, hard, new. The ground is covered in petals and from among them, life pushes upward. The tree gives and the ground receives and something new begins. No text.",
            "ja": "木。花びらが落ちたところに緑の球体が育つ。果実が形成されている。小さく、硬く、新しい。地面は花びらで覆われ、その間から生命が上に押し上がる。木が与え、大地が受け取り、何か新しいものが始まる。テキストなし。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
